  "term": "FTD",
  "definition": "FTD stands for frontotemporal dementia, a clinical syndrome and a common cause of early-onset dementia. It can appear mainly as behavioral changes, such as disinhibition, perseveration, inappropriate behavior, and marked personality change, or mainly as language problems such as aphasia.",
